em. ### The Bottom Line The second law *is* a strict law—for isolated systems. It is not a "mere tendency" because for any isolated macroscopic system, you will never see a spontaneous entropy decrease. The fact that Earth is not isolated does not make the law weak; it means you must apply the law to the correct system (the Sun-Earth-space combined system). In that combined system, entropy increases without exception. So no, the second law is not just a guideline. It is an absolute statistical law for its proper domain. Life's local order is not a violation of that law—it's a perfectly legal, predicted consequence of the Sun's energy flow.
